# Shared environment variables for the Next.js UI and Express API belong here.
# Copy this file to .env at the repository root.
#
# scripts/validate-env.mjs treats this file as the manifest of what has to be
# set, and `ui`, `deploy-ui`, and `e2e` all check it before doing any work. A
# variable is required in every mode by default; a marker comment scopes
# everything after it, until the next marker:
#
#   # @all               required in every mode (the default)
#   # @development-only  required for local work, not for a deploy
#   # @production-only   required for a deploy, not locally
#   # @test-only         required only by `npm run e2e`
#   # @optional          documented, never required
#
# Reach for @development-only when staging and prod read a secret from a file
# under /home/ecarlson10/pw/ rather than from the environment — otherwise a
# deploy would demand a variable production never reads. Note that `test`
# implies development, since the e2e suite drives the local dev stack.
#
# Everything below is an inert example: the extra leading "#" keeps both the
# markers and the assignments from being parsed, so a fresh clone requires
# nothing and `npm run ui` works out of the box. Uncomment what you need.
#
#   SOME_SHARED_SECRET=
#
#   # @development-only
#   STRIPE_TEST_SECRET_KEY=
#
#   # @test-only
#   E2E_EMAIL=
#   E2E_PASSWORD=
#
#   # @optional
#   SOME_FEATURE_FLAG=
